<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enrique Líster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907–1994</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enrique Líster was a Spanish Communist commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a>, a former stonemason who rose to lead the 11th Division and later an army corps of the Republic. In August 1937 his troops dissolved the anarchist Regional Defence <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-aragon">Council of Aragon</a>, arresting its leaders and breaking up collectives. After the war he lived in exile, mainly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, and returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> after Franco's death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enrique-lister.jpg" alt="Enrique Líster" width="190" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kitsuuu · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enrique_L%C3%ADster_1936.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
